  "description": "The target community is individuals familiar with U.S. political debates, particularly those who follow or are aware of the 2020 Democratic primary candidates (Elizabeth Warren, Bernie Sanders, Cory Booker). The meme relies on cultural references to political discourse, the use of sarcastic meme formats, and the stereotype of politicians being obsessed with 'free stuff' to create humor. This audience understands the context of the debate, the translation of the Spanish phrase, and the mocking tone intended to ridicule the candidates' policy focus.",
